We investigated the CS LAN default gateway 192.168.2.1 on router0 (interface eth1) and found no evidence of link flaps or overload. Router0’s eth1 is up and stable: carrier_changes=2 (only the expected up events at boot), operstate=up, and no RX/TX errors or drops (ip -s link show dev eth1; ifconfig). EtHtool reports link detected with 10G/full duplex. On the L2 side, switch1 (which connects router0.eth1 on eth0 to the CS LAN on eth1) shows both ports in forwarding state with zero errors and stable MAC learning; the gateway MAC a6:7f:36:6e:60:36 is learned consistently on switch1 eth0 towards router0 (bridge fdb show). Switch dmesg shows only initial STP transitions at startup, not recurring topology changes.

